{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118807","id":3561171589,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc7UQyqF","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118807","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118807.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118807.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118807","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118807/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118807/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118807/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/af9e6261e24fc5635348d1f6780fe8d0b0c37332","number":118807,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"[Core] Try to explicitly get StringName in `_call_bind`","user":{"login":"NoctemCat","id":22471296,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDcxMjk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22471296?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat","html_url":"https://github.com/NoctemCat","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoctemCat/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Original PR: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118507\r\n\r\n`_call_bind` multi-threaded debug improvements depends on https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118803.\r\nImproves multi-threaded speed of `_call_bind` in release build.\r\n\r\n## Technical overview\r\nExplicitly tries to get reference to the string name if the Variant is string name.\r\n\r\nI tried to use ternary \r\n```cpp\r\nconst StringName &method = (p_args[0]->get_type() == Variant::STRING_NAME) ? *VariantInternal::get_string_name(p_args[0])  : static_cast<StringName>(*VariantInternal::get_string(p_args[0]));\r\n```\r\nto have less changes, but it didn't improve anything, so the current PR handles them separately.\r\n\r\nOnly improves speed if the variant is `StringName`, if it is `String` the speed will be the same as in the current master. Tbh not sure if it is possible to pass `String` here, but it will handle it correctly.\r\n\r\n## Performace testing\r\nBuild commands are the same as in the original PR.\r\nTest project: [testthreads4.6_target.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26926113/testthreads4.6_target.zip)\r\n\r\nThe basic test was to divide the iterations between threads and to perform the most basic interaction inside the loop, in theory this should imitate doing parallelizable work. The number of iterations was 200_000_000.\r\n\r\nThe results are presented as tables. In the columns was written the number of threads this attempt used, 0th thread is main thread that serves as the control.\r\nColumn type:\r\n- `debug` - tested it in launched from Godot project\r\n- `tool` - tested it inside tool script in editor\r\n- `release` - tested it in export release\r\n\r\nTested on:\r\n- EndeavourOS on X11 \r\n- X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors \r\n- Vulkan (Forward+) \r\n- dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1650 (nvidia; 595.58.03) \r\n- Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-9300H CPU @ 2.40GHz (8 threads) \r\n- 15.49 GiB memory\r\n\r\nIncludes additional case with lock-free `ObjectDB::get_instance` on top of current changes. \r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>func_base, this one is fine, control</summary>\r\nSetting values directly on the instance fields is also fine\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nfunc func_base(count: int) -> int:\r\n    var time_before: int = Time.get_ticks_msec()\r\n    var sum := 0\r\n    for i in count:\r\n        sum += 1\r\n    finished.emit.call_deferred(Time.get_ticks_msec() - time_before)\r\n    return sum\r\n```\r\n\r\nfunc_base\r\n| Type    | Branch               |     0 |     1 |     2 |     3 |     4 |     5 |     6 |     7 |     8 |\r\n| ------- | -------------------- | ----: | ----: | ----: | ----: | ----: | ----: | ----: | ----: | ----: |\r\n| debug   | master               |  4022 |  4720 |  4214 |  3639 |  3602 |  3768 |  2999 |  2409 |  2896 |\r\n| debug   | call_bind            |  4159 |  4599 |  4181 |  3980 |  4424 |  4203 |  3201 |  2561 |  3494 |\r\n| debug   | call_bind.lock_free  |  3873 |  4283 |  3597 |  3909 |  3931 |  3480 |  2846 |  2850 |  2285 |\r\n| tool    | master               |  3900 |  3626 |  1957 |  1492 |  1141 |  1219 |  1141 |  1079 |  1030 |\r\n| tool    | call_bind            |  3614 |  3919 |  1988 |  1332 |  1162 |  1224 |  1159 |  1163 |  1055 |\r\n| tool    | call_bind.lock_free  |  3409 |  3615 |  1811 |  1423 |  1062 |  1173 |  1079 |  1096 |  1094 |\r\n| release | master               |  2539 |  3034 |  1445 |  1083 |  1221 |  1130 |  1063 |   805 |   694 |\r\n| release | call_bind            |  2463 |  2843 |  1501 |  1056 |  1129 |  1484 |   916 |   867 |   671 |\r\n| release | call_bind.lock_free  |  2563 |  2961 |  1579 |  1057 |  1183 |  1020 |   805 |  1001 |   686 |\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>call_bind, kind of strange</summary>\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nfunc call_bind(count: int) -> int:\r\n    var time_before: int = Time.get_ticks_msec()\r\n    var sum := 0\r\n    for i in count:\r\n        sum += call(&\"get_instance_increment\")\r\n    finished.emit.call_deferred(Time.get_ticks_msec() - time_before)\r\n    return sum\r\n\r\nfunc get_instance_increment() -> int:\r\n    return 1\r\n```\r\n\r\ncall_bind\r\n| Type    | Branch               |     0 |     1 |     2 |     3 |     4 |     5 |     6 |     7 |     8 |\r\n| ------- | -------------------- | ----: | ----: | ----: | ----: | ----: | ----: | ----: | ----: | ----: |\r\n| debug   | master               | 25835 | 29700 | 35301 | 35611 | 43392 | 44844 | 47641 | 47517 | 53493 |\r\n| debug   | call_bind            | 23792 | 26420 | 31817 | 34871 | 46004 | 45412 | 46411 | 49550 | 53029 |\r\n| debug   | call_bind.lock_free  | 22328 | 23339 | 18426 | 15541 | 14159 | 13648 | 12035 | 10919 |  9827 |\r\n| tool    | master               | 23172 | 23774 | 32148 | 32983 | 43708 | 42829 | 43810 | 46232 | 50544 |\r\n| tool    | call_bind            | 23374 | 24166 | 28399 | 34467 | 43967 | 42182 | 41480 | 43998 | 49790 |\r\n| tool    | call_bind.lock_free  | 19432 | 20295 | 10183 |  7862 |  6305 |  6961 |  6686 |  6678 |  6732 |\r\n| release | master               | 15362 | 17265 | 16623 | 16900 | 18178 | 18241 | 18002 | 17896 | 18325 |\r\n| release | call_bind            | 13954 | 15439 |  8375 |  6369 |  5811 |  6052 |  5967 |  5043 |  4801 |\r\n| release | call_bind.lock_free  | 14149 | 16318 |  9390 |  7100 |  6330 |  6729 |  6279 |  5664 |  5733 |\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nRaw results:\r\n[results_raw.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26926335/results_raw.txt)\r\n[results_grouped.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26926339/results_grouped.txt)\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":32409